  "page": 1,
  "citation": "nearly all progress happens within the first 30 of 100 questions, which largely decide how the game ends; after that, most models plateau"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-03",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "we find that the bottleneck is generation, not judgment: models recognize a good idea or a good question when one is offered, but often cannot produce it on their own"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-04",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "models fail by either over-exploiting one direction or over-exploring too many"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-05",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "enriching the search with externally sourced ideas and questions may be more effective than improving any single model's generation ability"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-06",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "an answerer model reads the full paper and replies to the questions"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-07",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "most progress happens within the first 30 questions, after which gains slow sharply for all but GPT-5.4, and a model's score at question 30 largely predicts its final score"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-08",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
  "empreinte": "ae848c68e65c4a779d0df6725e4189ad80c351fe2e9402930be14db2ddfa7ccc",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "on papers where both a strong and a weak model can list the core idea beforehand, the strong model still finishes far ahead"
 },
 {
  "id": "RS-09",
  "piece": "Re-Search, arXiv 2611.14487v1",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/organisme-re-search-v1/arxiv-2611.14487/2611.14487v1.pdf",
